                                    Create PDF Documents with Pages of Other PDF Documents
                                </td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td style="width: 100%;">

                                    <table style="width: 535px; height: 967px">
                                        <tbody>
                                            <tr>
                                                <td style="vertical-align: top">
                                                    <table>
                                                        <tbody>
                                                            <tr>
                                                                <td>
                                                                    Use this demo to draw the pages of existing PDF documents in a PDF document created with the PDF creator, with the
                                                                    PdfPageElement object. The letterhead page is drawn under the content of each page and the pages of the source document
                                                                    are drawn as scaled copies, with their links and form fields when the annotations are included. A drawn page can be rotated
                                                                    around a pivot point and can have an opacity. The last page draws the first page of the source document at its own size.
                                                                </td>
                                                            </tr>
                                                            <tr>
                                                                <td style="height: 12px"></td>
                                                            </tr>
                                                            <tr>
                                                                <td>
